---
import SEOHead from '../../../components/SEOHead.astro';
import GameNav from '../../../components/GameNav.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import SideAd from '../../../components/SideAd.astro';
import InContentAd from '../../../components/InContentAd.astro';
import LevelSelector from '../../../components/LevelSelector.astro';

const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 Walkthrough: Driveway";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 walkthrough for Driveway: the red sedan with plate 18-D-12345 and its light-control stalk set to AUTO, the lion's memorial tablet reading WILLIAM FOSTER / DIED / Oct. 7, 1866 / Aged 59 Years, the statue hint \"Pay attention to the lines on the statue\", the five-slider valve panel, the paper marked Valve handle position, the door labelled A17, and the skeleton key that finishes the level. There is no numeric keypad anywhere in this room; the reads below were each checked twice from separate frames.";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What is the code in Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 Driveway?",
    a: "There is no typed code. We sampled all 283 seconds of this recording and no keypad, dial bank or number panel ever appears — the only inputs are a car light-control stalk, a five-slider valve panel and a pipe network with red levers. The three pieces of text people mistake for codes are labels: the <b>18-D-12345</b> number plate on the red sedan, the <b>A17</b> plate on the mansion's front door, and the memorial tablet under the lion's paw, which reads <b>WILLIAM FOSTER / DIED / Oct. 7, 1866 / Aged 59 Years</b>.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a keypad in the Driveway?",
    a: "No. Frame by frame across the whole clip there is no keypad, no safe dial and no letter lock. Driveway is one of the chapter's outdoor rooms, and its interactives are physical: the car's light stalk, the valve panel between the two lion statues, and the pipe-and-valve network. If you are hunting for a four-digit pad, that is why you cannot find one.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does the memorial tablet under the lion say?",
    a: "The tablet held under the near lion's paw is engraved with four lines: <b>WILLIAM FOSTER</b>, <b>DIED</b>, <b>Oct. 7, 1866</b>, <b>Aged 59 Years</b>. We read it three ways — the whole frame at 0:56, a 3.4× crop of the tablet, and a wide 2.2× crop that included the paw and the base — and all three passes agreed. The date and the age are the two numbers worth writing down.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does the statue hint say?",
    a: "At roughly 2:21 a caption appears over the cherub statue on its fluted pedestal: <b>PAY ATTENTION TO THE LINES ON THE STATUE / AND TAKE THE LAST VALUE HANDLE</b>. It is printed as \"value\", which is the game's own typo for <b>valve</b> — and the item you get is literally called <b>Valve handle</b>. So the line is telling you two things: count or read the grooves on the pedestal, and take the last valve handle you find.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the five-slider panel between the lions?",
    a: "A metal service panel mounted in the wall between the two lion statues, with <b>five vertical sliders</b>, a row of square indicator lights down each side, and a single <b>horizontal slider</b> along the bottom. The <b>Piece of paper</b> in your inventory — the one labelled <b>Valve handle position</b> — is its clue: the paper is a hand-drawn schematic of five circles with an X through them, wired together with arrows. The panel is a valve bank, not a keypad: you are matching handle positions, not typing digits.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I get through the gate?",
    a: "Not with a code, and not at the start. At roughly 1:15 the camera moves to the gateway and a pale left-pointing arrow floats beside it — that arrow is the level's exit marker and it stays there for the rest of the run. It is a signpost rather than a lock, and tapping the gate early does nothing. The gate is dealt with last: the recording selects the <b>skeleton key</b> from the inventory at about 4:39, uses it, and the <b>LEVEL COMPLETED!</b> card follows at 4:42.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the A17 door?",
    a: "The mansion's front door, up the driveway past the fountain, carries a plate reading <b>A17</b>. Read twice — the OCR pass and a 1.9× crop of the door both give A17, and the plate is set centrally on the dark wooden door between its glazed panels. A later hint at about 3:41 reads <b>BACK TO THE A17 ON THE DOOR</b>, which is the game sending you back to that door rather than naming a code.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the pipe puzzle with the red levers?",
    a: "A full-screen network of grey pipe segments joined by flanges, with <b>red lever handles</b> at the junctions and a <b>green flow indicator</b> in the lower right. The recording works it between roughly 3:30 and 3:45 and returns to it later. It behaves like the standard flow puzzle: turn the valves so the run connects through to the green lamp. We are not printing a lever-by-lever list, because the clip is sped up and cut and a half-right order would cost you more time than working it out.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does the car's light stalk do?",
    a: "Inside the sedan, the left stalk behind the wheel is a rotary light switch with four markings, top to bottom: <b>O</b> (off), <b>AUTO</b>, a parking-light symbol, and a headlight symbol. In the recording the dial sits on <b>AUTO</b>, and that is the state the level wants — we read the stalk twice, whole frame and a 1.7× crop, and both reads put the pointer on AUTO. The right-hand rocker on the same stalk carries the front and rear fog-light symbols.",
  },
  {
    q: "What ends the level?",
    a: "A <b>skeleton key</b>. The inventory at the end holds two items — the car key fob and an old-fashioned key — and the recording selects the key, uses it at the gate, and the level completes. The gate is the level exit: the outline-arrow icon sits on the gateway itself, and the results card follows about a second later.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is Driveway room 12 of Chapter 3?",
    a: "Yes. Chapter 3 is <i>Murder Dressed in White</i> and its fifteen rooms run: Dining Room, Living Room, Study Room, Guest Toilet, Workshop, Guest Bedroom, Master Bathroom, Kids Playroom, Backyard, Garden, Kitchen, <b>Driveway</b>, Kids Bedroom 1, Storage Room, Garage. Driveway is room <b>12 of 15</b>, directly after Kitchen and before Kids Bedroom 1.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does the recording show the level being completed?",
    a: "Yes — this is the first room in the chapter where our copy includes the ending. The card reads <b>LEVEL COMPLETED!</b> at about 4:42. What it does not show is a reward figure: the card carries the title and two rule lines and nothing else, and our copy ends on that frame, so this page prints no coin amount for Driveway.",
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, "") },
  })),
};
