<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; Chapter 3 &gt; Level 12</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 Walkthrough: Driveway</h1>

    <p>Driveway is the twelfth room of Chapter 3, <i>Murder Dressed in White</i> — the last of the chapter's outdoor rooms, following Garden and leading back inside to Kids Bedroom 1. It starts outside a walled mansion entrance at night: a shut wrought-iron gate, a red sedan parked nose-in with the number plate <b>18-D-12345</b>, two stone lions on pedestals looking down at the driveway, and a circular fountain further up the herringbone paving. There is no keypad here — that is the single most useful thing to know before you start tapping things.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame at one frame per second across the full 4:42 clip, including the ending. Every piece of text printed as a read on this page was checked at least twice from separate frames — the memorial tablet three ways, the <b>A17</b> plate twice, the statue caption twice, plate <b>18-D-12345</b> twice. Anything that only resolved once, or that two passes read differently, is listed under "What this page could not verify" instead of being stated as fact.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={3} current={12} variant="jump" label="Chapter 3 · Murder Dressed in White" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>Driveway is room 12 of 15 in Chapter 3. There is <b>no typed code</b> in this level — no keypad appears anywhere in the recording. The four things that matter are:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><b>A17</b> — the plate on the mansion's front door. A later hint sends you <b>back to the A17 on the door</b>; it is a location, not a code to enter.</li>
        <li><b>AUTO</b> — the position of the car's light-control stalk. Read twice; the dial sits on AUTO with O, the parking-light and headlight symbols above and below it.</li>
        <li><b>WILLIAM FOSTER / DIED / Oct. 7, 1866 / Aged 59 Years</b> — the memorial tablet under the lion's paw. The date and age are the only real numbers in the room.</li>
        <li><b>Five-slider valve panel</b> between the two lions, plus the pipe network with red levers. The <b>Piece of paper</b> in your bag (labelled <b>Valve handle position</b>) is the clue: five X-marked circles wired with arrows. Match handles, do not type digits.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>End of the level: pick up the <b>skeleton key</b>, select it in the inventory, use it at the gate, and the <b>LEVEL COMPLETED!</b> card appears at about 4:42.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
      <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="zpx_qJcWbBc" data-title="Rooms &amp; Exits Level 12 Driveway Walkthrough Murder Dressed in White Chapter 3"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp; Exits Level 12 Driveway Walkthrough">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/zpx_qJcWbBc/maxresdefault.jpg"
             alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 Driveway walkthrough video" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1280" height="720"
             onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://i.ytimg.com/vi/zpx_qJcWbBc/hqdefault.jpg'">
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="video-cap">The 4:42 Driveway run used for every frame on this page — the in-game clock in the corner runs faster than the video, so ignore the timer in the screenshots.</p>

    <img class="hero" src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-fountain-running.jpg" alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 Driveway: the Mediterranean mansion seen across its circular drive, the stone fountain running in the middle, the red sedan parked by the steps and the iron entrance gate on the right" width="1200" height="594" />

    <h2>What this level actually is<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>One outdoor area, three separate puzzle sites. The entrance end has the gate and the two lions with their memorial tablet; the middle has the circular driveway, the working fountain and the parked sedan; the house end has the front door marked <b>A17</b>, a bench with a duffel bag, and a cherub statue on a fluted pedestal in a small lawn. Everything is reachable by tapping, and the camera swings between a wide property view and tight one-object views with the usual white corner brackets.</p>
    <p>The puzzle logic is physical rather than numeric, which is why the room feels different from Kitchen. The car's light stalk is a rotary switch you turn; the metal panel between the lions is a bank of five sliders; the pipe network is a set of red levers you flip until flow reaches a green lamp. Nothing in this level asks you to type a number, and nothing asks you to spell a word.</p>
    <p>What the room does have is one very readable piece of prose on stone. The near lion rests its paw on an upright tablet, and the tablet is engraved with a name, a death date and an age. In a chapter that has so far hidden its clues on notes and mugs, carving them into a gravestone is a nice piece of theatre — and it is the one clue in Driveway you can read at a glance.</p>

    <h2>The map: what is where<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Everything we could identify, and what it is for.</p>
    <table class="item-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Object</th><th>Where</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Wrought-iron gate</td><td>Entrance end of the driveway</td><td>Where the level ends. A pale left-pointing arrow — the exit marker — floats beside it from about 1:15 onward.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Red sedan</td><td>Parked facing the gate</td><td>Plate <b>18-D-12345</b>. Enter it for the light-control stalk puzzle; later a car key fob is in your inventory.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Light-control stalk</td><td>Left of the steering wheel, inside the car</td><td>Rotary dial marked <b>O</b>, <b>AUTO</b>, parking-light symbol, headlight symbol. Sits on <b>AUTO</b>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Two stone lions</td><td>On pedestals flanking the gate</td><td>Frame the entrance. The near lion's paw rests on the memorial tablet.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Memorial tablet</td><td>Under the near lion's paw</td><td>Engraved <b>WILLIAM FOSTER / DIED / Oct. 7, 1866 / Aged 59 Years</b>. The room's clearest written clue.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Five-slider valve panel</td><td>Wall between the two lions</td><td>Five vertical sliders, square indicator rows down both sides, a horizontal slider along the bottom.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Piece of paper</td><td>Inventory item</td><td>Labelled <b>Valve handle position</b>. Hand-drawn schematic: five circles with an X through each, joined by arrows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pipe network</td><td>Full-screen puzzle</td><td>Grey pipe segments, <b>red lever handles</b> at junctions, <b>green flow indicator</b> lower right.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cherub statue</td><td>Circular lawn right of the driveway</td><td>On a fluted pedestal. Raises the caption about the lines on the statue.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bench</td><td>Against the house wall</td><td>Wooden slats on ornate iron legs, with a duffel bag and a furled umbrella on it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Front door A17</td><td>Mansion entrance, up the driveway</td><td>Dark wooden door with glazed panels and a central <b>A17</b> plate. The hint later sends you back to it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Skeleton key</td><td>Inventory, near the end</td><td>The last item collected. Select it, choose Use, and the gate ends the level.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Step by step<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The order below follows the recording. Timestamps are video time; the links jump to the matching second.</p>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 · 0:02</span>
      <strong>Read the entrance before you touch it</strong>
      The level opens on the entrance with no cutscene: a dark iron gate between stone pillars, lanterns burning overhead, a lion on its pedestal to one side, and the red sedan parked facing away from you with <b>18-D-12345</b> on its plate. Sweep once — gate ahead, lion and paving underfoot, hedges along the walls — then get into the car.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-hero-driveway.jpg" alt="The near stone lion holding its shield on a pedestal, the herringbone driveway and the rear of the red sedan at the entrance in Driveway" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=2s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:02</a></div>
    </div>
    <InContentAd />

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 · 0:30 · inside the car</span>
      <strong>The light-control stalk is already on AUTO</strong>
      Tapping the sedan puts you behind the wheel. The interactive part is the left stalk: a rotary dial with four markings, top to bottom <b>O</b>, <b>AUTO</b>, a parking-light symbol and a headlight symbol, and the pointer sits on <b>AUTO</b>. The right-hand rocker on the same stalk carries the front and rear fog-light symbols. We read this twice — the whole frame and a 1.7× crop — and both reads put the pointer on AUTO, so if your dial has been spun elsewhere, that is the setting to restore.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-car-light-stalk.jpg" alt="The car light-control stalk inside the red sedan in Driveway, with the rotary dial on AUTO and the off, parking-light and headlight markings above and below" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=30s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:30</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3 · 0:44 · the dashboard</span>
      <strong>The cabin is a second, quieter view</strong>
      The camera pulls back to the whole dashboard: three-spoke wheel, two backlit gauges, a centre screen showing a map and a row of climate controls under it. Nothing here is an input — this is the game letting you look around the interior after the stalk. The car key fob is already listed as a carried item by this point, and it is still in the bag at the end.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-car-dashboard.jpg" alt="The dashboard of the red sedan in Driveway: steering wheel, instrument gauges and centre navigation screen" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=44s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:44</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 · 0:56 · the memorial tablet</span>
      <strong>WILLIAM FOSTER, died Oct. 7, 1866, aged 59</strong>
      The near lion holds an upright tablet under its paw, and the tablet is engraved in four lines: <b>WILLIAM FOSTER</b>, <b>DIED</b>, <b>Oct. 7, 1866</b>, <b>Aged 59 Years</b>. Above the text there is a small carved medallion. Of everything written in Driveway, this is the clearest read and the only place two usable numbers appear — the year 1866 and the age 59. Write both down before you leave the gate.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-lion-memorial-tablet.jpg" alt="The memorial tablet under the lion's paw in Driveway, engraved William Foster, died Oct. 7 1866, aged 59 years" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=56s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:56</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5 · 1:15 · the gateway</span>
      <strong>The gate area, and the arrow that sits on it all level</strong>
      The camera returns to the gateway end of the drive: two stone pillars, the wrought-iron leaves between them, hedges along the wall and the lamp still burning. A pale left-pointing arrow floats in the dark HUD strip beside the gateway — that icon is the level's exit marker, and it is there from the middle of the run right through to the end. It is a signpost, not a lock: there is nothing to tap on the gate at this stage.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-gate-open-arrow.jpg" alt="The gateway in Driveway with its stone pillars and iron leaves, and the pale left-pointing exit arrow beside it" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=75s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:15</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 · 1:30 · the bench</span>
      <strong>A duffel bag and a furled umbrella</strong>
      Along the house wall sits a slatted wooden bench on ornate iron legs, with a brown-and-blue duffel bag on the seat and a closed umbrella leaning on the left armrest. The bench, bag and umbrella all outline as interactive. This is where the room's tools start arriving — the bag is worth opening before you go back to the gate.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-bench-duffel-bag.jpg" alt="The wooden bench against the house wall in Driveway with a duffel bag on the seat and a furled umbrella at the armrest" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=90s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:30</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 · 2:22 · the statue caption</span>
      <strong>"Pay attention to the lines on the statue"</strong>
      The cherub on its fluted pedestal raises a two-line caption across the top of the screen: <b>PAY ATTENTION TO THE LINES ON THE STATUE / AND TAKE THE LAST VALUE HANDLE</b>. The second line is printed as "value" — the game's own typo for <b>valve</b>, confirmed by the item you receive, which is called <b>Valve handle</b>. Read it as two instructions: study the pedestal's grooves, and pick up the last valve handle.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-statue-hint-popup.jpg" alt="The Driveway statue hint reading pay attention to the lines on the statue and take the last value handle" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=142s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2:22</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 2:48 · the valve panel</span>
      <strong>Five sliders, not five digits</strong>
      Between the two lions there is a metal service panel: <b>five vertical sliders</b> with rounded tracks, a column of small square indicators down each side, and a single <b>horizontal slider</b> running along the bottom between two sets of three short lines. The recording works it from about 2:30 to 3:00. It is a valve bank — each slider is a handle position, which is exactly what the paper in your bag is describing.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-valve-panel.jpg" alt="The five-slider valve panel between the two lion statues in Driveway, with a horizontal slider along the bottom" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=168s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2:48</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 9 · 3:20 · the paper</span>
      <strong>"Valve handle position"</strong>
      In the inventory, examine the <b>Piece of paper</b>. The item label under it reads <b>Valve handle position</b>, and the drawing is a hand-drawn schematic: five circles each crossed with an X, joined by straight runs of line with small arrows showing direction, and small square terminals at the ends. That is the valve bank drawn as a circuit. If you are stuck on the panel, this paper is the only place the arrangement is written down.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-paper-valve-diagram.jpg" alt="The Piece of paper in Driveway labelled Valve handle position, showing five crossed circles joined by arrows" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=200s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3:20</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 · 3:42 · the pipe network</span>
      <strong>Red levers, one green lamp</strong>
      A full-screen pipe puzzle: grey segments joined by flanges, <b>red lever handles</b> standing at the junctions, and a <b>green flow indicator</b> glowing in the lower right corner. The recording turns handles here, leaves, and comes back to it later. The goal is the usual one — get the run connected through to the green lamp — and we are deliberately not printing a lever order, because the footage is sped up and cut and a wrong sequence would waste more of your time than working it out.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-pipe-puzzle.jpg" alt="The pipe and valve network puzzle in Driveway with red lever handles and a green flow indicator" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=222s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3:42</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 11 · 4:07 · the A17 door</span>
      <strong>The plate on the front door, and the hint that sends you back</strong>
      The mansion's front door is dark wood with glazed panels either side of a central plate reading <b>A17</b>. A caption a little earlier reads <b>BACK TO THE A17 ON THE DOOR</b> — so the game is treating A17 as a destination, not a combination. We read the plate twice, the OCR pass and a 1.9× crop of the door, and both give A17.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-door-a17.jpg" alt="The mansion front door in Driveway with the plate A17 mounted centrally on the dark wooden panels" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=247s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:07</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 12 · 4:39 to 4:42 · the key and the gate</span>
      <strong>Skeleton key, Use, then LEVEL COMPLETED!</strong>
      The last two inventory items are the car key fob and an old-fashioned <b>skeleton key</b>. The recording selects the key, chooses <b>Use</b>, and the gateway is where the interaction lands: the pale exit arrow is sitting beside the gate, the camera holds there, and the <b>LEVEL COMPLETED!</b> card follows at about 4:42. The card carries the title and two rule lines only — our copy ends on that frame, so there is no coin figure to report.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l12-level-completed.jpg" alt="The LEVEL COMPLETED card at the end of Rooms and Exits Chapter 3 Level 12 Driveway" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=279s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:39</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpx_qJcWbBc&t=282s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:42</a></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Where people get stuck<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p><b>You keep looking for a keypad.</b> There isn't one. Driveway is one of the chapter's outdoor rooms and every input in it is physical: a rotary stalk, five sliders, a bank of pipe levers. If you are stuck because you cannot find somewhere to type the year on the gravestone, the answer is that no such place exists — the tablet is atmosphere with a usable number in it, not a code to enter here.</p>
    <p><b>The gate will not open when you tap it early.</b> It is not meant to. From about 1:15 there is a pale left-pointing arrow floating beside the gateway — that is the exit marker, and it is showing you where the level finishes, not inviting you to try the gate now. The gate becomes usable at the very end, after the skeleton key is in your bag.</p>
    <p><b>The valve panel looks like a combination lock.</b> Five sliders in a row reads as five digits if you are coming straight from a keypad room, and then you cannot work out what the numbers should be, because there are no numbers. The panel is a valve bank: the sliders are handle heights, and the <b>Piece of paper</b> labelled <b>Valve handle position</b> is the diagram that tells you which handle goes where.</p>
    <p><b>The statue caption says "value handle" and you cannot find a value handle.</b> That is a typo in the game's own text. The item you are meant to take is the <b>Valve handle</b>, and the panel between the lions is where it belongs.</p>
    <p><b>The pipe puzzle never lights green.</b> The green lamp is in the lower right of the network, so trace from there backwards rather than from the top. The red levers at the junctions are the parts that change the route; the plain flanged segments are fixed.</p>

    <h2>Where Driveway sits in Chapter 3<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Chapter 3 is <i>Murder Dressed in White</i>, and its fifteen rooms run: Dining Room, Living Room, Study Room, Guest Toilet, Workshop, Guest Bedroom, Master Bathroom, Kids Playroom, Backyard, Garden, Kitchen, <b>Driveway</b>, Kids Bedroom 1, Storage Room, Garage. Driveway is room <b>12 of 15</b>, straight after the Kitchen and immediately before Kids Bedroom 1.</p>
    <p>It is also the chapter's change of scenery. Kitchen is a dense indoor room with four puzzle types stacked on three walls; Driveway opens the camera out, drops the keypad entirely and gives you a car, a gate, a gravestone and a fountain instead. If you have just finished Kitchen, expect the pace to feel slower and the clues to feel more spread out — the walk between the gate, the bench and the front door is most of the level.</p>

